- How would you test runtime-loaded handlers?
- How would you handle type-safety for diverse payload schemas across handlers?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of a small, runtime-extendable data pipeline using common patterns. It’s approachable for beginners and maps to real-world data processing tasks.

## Key Concepts

- Registry pattern
- Pipeline/Chain execution
- Runtime extensibility and isolation
- Error handling and testing

## Code Example

```javascript
interface Transformer { transform(input: any): any; }
class Registry {
  private map = new Map<string, () => Transformer>();
  register(name: string, factory: () => Transformer) { this.map.set(name, factory); }
  create(name: string): Transformer | undefined { const f = this.map.get(name); return f ? f() : undefined; }
}
class Pipeline {
  constructor(private registry: Registry, private steps: string[]) {}
  run(input: any): any {
    let data = input;
    for (const name of this.steps) {
      const t = this.registry.create(name);
      if (!t) throw new Error(`Unknown transformer: ${name}`);
      data = t.transform(data);
    }
    return data;
  }
}
```

